ublox.c and novatel.c are T. Takasu's, the holder of license.txt: BSD 2-clause for them is an
inference from the distribution. septentrio.c, rt17.c and unicore.c carry no licence header of their
own and name other authors; they are distributed with RTKLIB-EX, whose licence as a whole is the BSD
2-clause of license.txt, and are taken here on that basis, by the decision of the maintainer of this
package (2026-11-10), with their copyright lines kept as they are. RT-17 carries the time of the week
only (an approximate time of the log is needed, as for RTCM 3). The entry points that rcvraw.c calls for
the other receivers are stubs of ours in native/src/rcv_stubs.c, which decode nothing; ppg_convbin()
does not take those formats. RTCM 3 needs no file of src/rcv: rtcm.c and rtcm3.c decode it.

RINEX is never an input of convrnx() here (ppg_convbin() takes u-blox, RTCM 3, NovAtel, Septentrio,
RT-17 and Unicore only):
convrnx() would decompress a compressed RINEX file through a shell command (rtk_uncompress).

Also left out: src/sofa.c, which the makefile of rnx2rtkp lists. It is a bundle of routines of the
IAU SOFA library (epv00 and moon98 with the functions they need), and SOFA has a licence of its
own, not BSD: its notes, which the file refers to, are in lib/sofa/src of the upstream repository
and are not part of this package. rtkcmn.c calls the two functions only if SUNPOS_SOFA or
MOONPOS_SOFA is defined, an option for more accurate positions of the Sun and the Moon. Neither
is defined here (nor in the makefile of rnx2rtkp): sunpos_eci() and moonpos_eci() take RTKLIB's
own series (their #else branches), and nothing refers to sofa.c (rtkcmn.c only declares the two
functions). sunmoonpos() is reached from the tide corrections (tides.c), PPP (ppp.c) and the
satellite antenna offsets of precise ephemerides (preceph.c), none of which the post-processing
of this package uses. RTKLIB's sample data (a static and a kinematic run) gives the same solution
files, byte for byte, with and without it. Do not put it back, or define either macro, without
carrying the SOFA licence in this package.
